cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Plateau: a semantic circuit breaker for autonomous AI agents"
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to its measurements, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Akul
    family-names: Ranjan
    email: akulranjan06@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/AkulRanjan/Plateau-obs"
abstract: >-
  Plateau detects when an autonomous agent has stopped learning, rather than
  when it has started repeating itself. Each turn is read on two dials computed
  from local sentence embeddings: observation novelty against a window of recent
  observations, and action similarity. Novelty is the trip axis; similarity only
  sets the evidence bar, which lets a healthy batch job whose actions are nearly
  identical be distinguished from a stalled agent whose actions keep changing.
  No LLM API is involved in the decision path. Every figure published with this
  project is produced by a script in the repository and written to metrics.json,
  and a check fails the build if a documented number is not backed by a
  measurement.
keywords:
  - autonomous agents
  - circuit breaker
  - loop detection
  - information stagnation
  - sentence embeddings
  - agent observability
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-12"
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      TRAIL: Trace Reasoning and Agentic Issue Localization
    abstract: >-
      The expert-annotated agent-trace dataset used for this project's only
      measurements on real agent traces. Gated; never redistributed here.
    authors:
      - name: Patronus AI
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2505.08638"
        description: arXiv preprint identifier
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/PatronusAI/TRAIL"
